</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"55c5d3c2","external_id":"52a0019a-5b36-4d56-b8de-878dbc9fd5fd","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"8455e44c-2fd0-4cda-8d95-a1ca08ee36ab","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a Superscript x Baseline plus b\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> are constants and <math alttext=\"a greater than 0\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. In the <em>xy</em>-plane, the graph of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> has a <em>y</em>-intercept at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma negative 25 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> and passes through the point&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 2 comma 23 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"a plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>a</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["-19"],"correct_answer":["-19"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"negative 19\"><mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>19</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It's given that function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right p