    ($SATQ$565428e1$SATQ$, $SATQ$763bb625-3667-4ea6-af9f-195d80193bdb$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Equivalent expressions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="RootIndex 3 StartRoot p squared EndRoot equals t Superscript nine sevenths"><mroot><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>
<p>In the given equation, <math alttext="p greater than 1"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math alttext="t greater than 1"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. If <math alttext="t equals p Superscript 3 n minus 1"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, where <math alttext="n"><mi>n</mi>
</math> is a constant, what is the value of <math alttext="n"><mi>n</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$[".5061",".5062","41/81"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$[".5061",".5062","41/81"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 41 Over 81 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>41</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac></math>. An expression of the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="RootIndex n StartRoot a Superscript m Baseline EndRoot"><mroot><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mi>n</mi></mroot></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="m"><mi>m</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="n"><mi>n</mi></math> are integers greater than&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a greater than or equals 0"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, is equivalent to&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a Superscript StartFraction m Over n EndFraction"><msup><mi>a</mi><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msup></math>. Therefore, the expression on the left-hand side of the given equation is equivalent to&nbsp; <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="p Superscript two thirds"><msup><mi>p</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>; thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="p Superscript two thirds Baseline equals t Superscript nine sevenths"><msup><mi>p</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. If&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t equals p Superscript 3 n minus 1"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="n"><mi>n</mi></math> is a constant, then substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="p Superscript 3 n minus 1"><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math> in the equation yields&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="p Superscript two thirds Baseline equals p Superscript nine sevenths left parenthesis 3 n minus 1 right parenthesis"><msup><mi>p</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></math>. It's given that&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="p greater than 1"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>; therefore, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="two thirds equals nine sevenths left parenthesis 3 n minus 1 right parenthesis"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="21"><mn>21</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="14 equals 27 left parenthesis 3 n minus 1 right parenthesis"><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Distributing multiplication over subtraction yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="14 equals 81 n minus 27"><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></math>. Adding <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="27"><mn>27</mn></math> to each side of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="41 equals 81 n"><mn>41</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn><mi>n</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="81"><mn>81</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 41 Over 81 EndFraction equals n"><mfrac><mn>41</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></math>. Therefore, if <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t equals p Superscript 3 n minus 1"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="n"><mi>n</mi></math> is a constant, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="n"><mi>n</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 41 Over 81 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>41</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac></math>. Note that 41/81, .5061, .5062, and 0.506 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"565428e1","external_id":"763bb625-3667-4ea6-af9f-195d80193bdb","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"65ede589-a912-4bd7-8e08-e32875e7fa00","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.A.","skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"RootIndex 3 StartRoot p squared EndRoot equals t Superscript nine sevenths\"><mroot><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>\n<p>In the given equation, <math alttext=\"p greater than 1\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math alttext=\"t greater than 1\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. If <math alttext=\"t equals p Superscript 3 n minus 1\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, where <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math>