h xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi></math> is a constant, then substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p Superscript 3 n minus 1\"><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> in the equation yields&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p Superscript two thirds Baseline equals p Superscript nine sevenths left parenthesis 3 n minus 1 right parenthesis\"><msup><mi>p</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></math>. It's given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p greater than 1\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>; therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"two thirds equals nine sevenths left parenthesis 3 n minus 1 right parenthesis\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"14 equals 27 left parenthesis 3 n minus 1 right parenthesis\"><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Distributing multiplication over subtraction yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"14 equals 81 n minus 27\"><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></math>. Adding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn></math> to each side of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"41 equals 81 n\"><mn>41</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn><mi>n</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"81\"><mn>81</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 41 Over 81 EndFraction equals n\"><mfrac><mn>41</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></math>. Therefore, if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t equals p Superscript 3 n minus 1\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi></math> is a constant, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 41 Over 81 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>41</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac></math>. Note that 41/81, .5061, .5062, and 0.506 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1776362727992,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"565428e1","skill_cd":"P.A.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","createDate":1776362727992,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"763bb625-3667-4ea6-af9f-195d80193bdb","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"65ede589-a912-4bd7-8e08-e32875e7fa00","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"spr","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"RootIndex 3 StartRoot p squared EndRoot equals t Superscript nine sevenths\"><mroot><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>\n<p>In the given equation, <math alttext=\"p greater than 1\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math alttext=\"t g