xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5 x squared equals 5 x"><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5 x"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5 x squared minus 5 x equals 0"><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Factoring out a common factor of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5 x"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></math> from the left-hand side of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5 x left parenthesis x minus 1 right parenthesis equals 0"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. It follows that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5 x equals 0"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x minus 1 equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5 x equals 0"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 5 x plus 4"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 5 left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis plus 4"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 4"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Therefore, a solution to the given system of equations is the ordered pair <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 4 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>
