o>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x equals 0\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x minus 1 equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x equals 0\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 5 x plus 4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 5 left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis plus 4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Therefore, a solution to the given system of equations is the ordered pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 4 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"positio