/mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The second equation in the given system is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 5 x squared plus 4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x squared plus 4\"><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;in the first equation of the given system yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x squared plus 4 equals 5 x plus 4\"><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x squared equals 5 x\"><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x squared minus 5 x equals 0\"><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Factoring out a common factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></math> from the left-hand side of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x left parenthesis x minus 1 right parenthesis equals 0\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x equals 0\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x minus 1 equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x equals 0\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 5 x plus 4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 5 left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis plus 4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Therefore, a solution to the given system of equations is the ordered pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 4 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"8fd03417-fa6c-4681-901b-22278562189d","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1755117017721,"updateDate":1755117017721}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017721, 1755117017721),
    ($SATQ$58b109d4$SATQ$, $SATQ$7e4cd51c-5329-4e8b-83dd-1416f04a294f$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$11fad1ef-6f66-4959-b400-457b4f7204f0$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="x squared plus y plus 7 equals 7"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>y</mi>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>7</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>7</mn>
</mrow>
</math></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="20 x plus 100 minus y equals 0"><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The solution to the given system of equations is&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["-10"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["-10"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="negative 10"><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn>
</math>. Adding <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> to both sides of the second equation in the given system yields <math alttext="20 x plus 100 equals y"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>20</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>100</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>y</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="20 x plus 100"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>20</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>100</mn>
</mrow>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the first equation in the given system yields <math alttext="x squared plus 20 x plus 100 plus 7 equals 7"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="x squared plus 20 x plus 100 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>20</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>100</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Factoring the left-hand side of this equation yields <math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 10 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 10 right parenthesis equals 0"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, or <math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 10 right parenthesis squared equals 0"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="x plus 10 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>10</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="x equals negative 10"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="negative 10"><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"58b109d4","external_id":"7e4cd51c-5329-4e8b-83dd-1416f04a294f","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"11fad1ef-6f66-4959-b400-457b4f7204f0","uId":"ffff47cc-dc03-44d8-aa01-94f588a44fdb","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"x squared plus y plus 7 equals 7\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>7</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"20 x plus 100 minus y equals 0\"><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution to the given system of equations is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["-10"],"correct_answer":["-10"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"negative 10\"><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn>\n</math>. Adding <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> to both sides of the second equation in the given system yields <math alttext=\"20 x plus 100 equals y\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>20</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>100</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"20 x plus 100\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>20</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>100</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> in the first equation in the given system yields <math alttext=\"x squared plus 20 x plus 100 plus 7 equals 7\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"x squared plus 20 x plus 100 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>20</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>100</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Factoring the left-hand side of this equation yields <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 10 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 10 right parenthesis equals 0\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 10 right parenthesis squared equals 0\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"x plus 10 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>10</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 10\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"negative 10\"><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateD