xpression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_002_85dcf2e4.png\" alt=\"M equals 1,800 times, 1 point 0 0 5, to the power 4 q\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_003_e0cd2c52.png\" alt=\"M equals 1,800 times, 1 point 0 8 2, to the power q\"></span></span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. In 1 year, there are 4 quarter years, so the number of quarter years, <span class=\"italic\">q</span>, is 4 times the number of years, <span class=\"italic\">t</span> ; that is, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_005_624dee99.png\" alt=\"q, equals 4, t\"></span>. This is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_006_5e25668e.png\" alt=\" t equals, q over 4\"></span>, and substituting this into the expression for <span class=\"italic\">M</span> in terms of <span class=\"italic\">t</span> gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_007_3ffb923b.png\" alt=\"M equals, 1,800 times, 1 point 0 2 raised to the fraction q over 4 power\"></span>.<p>Choices B and D are incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly using <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_008_f2901bfe.png\" alt=\"t equals, 4 q\"></span> instead of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_009_624dee99.png\" alt=\"q, equals 4, t\"></span>. (Choices B and D are nearly the same since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_010_cdfed6bb.png\" alt=\"1 point 0 2 raised to the 4 q power\"></span> is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_011_12c9387a.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, 1 point 0 2 to the fourth power, close parenthesis, raised to the q power\"></span>, which is approximately <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_012_53cb8004.png\" alt=\"1 point 0 8 2 to the q power\"></span>.) Choice C is incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly using <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/59d1f4b5/img_013_f2901bfe.png\" alt=\"t equals, 4 q\"></span>&nbsp;and unnecessarily dividing 0.02 by 4.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":14,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959616,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"59d1f4b5","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1691007959616,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"019576-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"9406cedc-7041-4013-ba2f-338ee94bb04e","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"019576-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"M equals 1,800 times, 1 point 0 2, to the power t\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The equation above models the number of members,&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">M,</span> of a gym <span class=\"italic\">t</span> years after the gym opens. Of the following, which equation models the number of members of the gym <span class=\"italic\">q</span> quarter years after the gym opens?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"M equals 1,800 times, 1 point 0 2, to the power of the fraction q over 4\"></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"M equals 1,800 times, 1 point 0 2, to the power 4 q\"></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"M equals 1,800 times, 1 point 0 0 5, to the power 4 q\"></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"M equals 1,800 times, 1 point 0 8 2, to the power q\"></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. In 1 year, there are 4 quarter years, so the number of quarter years, <span class=\"italic\">q</span>, is 4 times the number of years, <span class=\"italic\">t</span> ; that is, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"q, equals 4, t\"></span>. This is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\" t equals, q over 4\"></span>, and substituting this into the expression for <span class=\"italic\">M</span> in terms of <span class=\"italic\">t</span> gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"M equals, 1,800 times, 1 point 0 2 raised to the fraction q over 4 power\"></span>.<p>Choices B and D are incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly using <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"t equals, 4 q\"></span> instead of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"q, equals 4, t\"></span>. (Choices B and D are nearly the same since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"1 point 0 2 raised to the 4 q power\"></span> is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, 1 point 0 2 to the fourth power, close parenthesis, raised to the q power\"></span>, which is approximately <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"1 point 0 8 2 to the q power\"></span>.) Choice C is incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly using <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"t equals, 4 q\"></span>&nbsp;and unnecessarily dividing 0.02 by 4.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959616,"updateDate":1691007959616}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959616, 1691007959616),
    ($SATQ$5a74f696$SATQ$, $SATQ$29fc6f6a-c78f-4294-a4fc-98e4343406e7$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">An investment account was opened with an initial value of <math alttext="dollar sign 890"><mo>$</mo><mn>890</mn></math>. The value of the account doubled every <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> years. Which equation represents the value of the account <math alttext="upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math>, in dollars, <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> years after the account was opened?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"5f17b802-8420-486d-ac0b-126552f676bc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 890 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction t Over 10 EndFraction\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>890</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"e5669886-17bd-45fc-aa43-f22e092badde","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 890 left parenthesis one tenth right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction t Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>890</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"1c886297-e228-4cf7-9343-8c7871190b5a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 890 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction t Over 10 EndFraction\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>890</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"e456ab4d-b285-46c6-97e1-67121dff517e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 890 left parenthesis 10 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction t Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>890</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>10</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["1c886297-e228-4cf7-9343-8c7871190b5a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. It's given that <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> represents the number of years since the account was opened. Therefore, <math alttext="StartFraction t Over 10 EndFraction"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math> represents the number of <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>-year periods since the account was opened. Since the value of the account doubles during each of these <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>-year periods, the value of the account can be found by multiplying the initial value by <math alttext="StartFraction t Over 10 EndFraction"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math> factors of <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>. This is equivalent to <math alttext="2 Superscript StartFraction t Over 10 EndFraction"><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. It's given that the initial value of the account is <math alttext="dollar sign 890"><mo>$</mo><mn>890</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of the account <math alttext="upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math>, in dollars, <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> years after the account was opened can be represented by <math alttext="upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 890 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction t Over 10 EndFraction"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>890</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac></msup></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents the value of an account if the value of the account halves, not doubles, every <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> years.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This equation represents the value of an account if the value of the account decreases by <math alttext="90 percent sign"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, not doubles, every <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>, years.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents the value of an account if the value of the account increases by a factor of <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>, not doubles, every <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>, years.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"5a74f696","external_id":"29fc6f6a-c78f-4294-a4fc-98e4343406e7","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"bf4b1638-4a60-45f7-a67a-4359230611cb","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">An investment account was opened with an initial value of <math alttext=\"dollar sign 890\"><mo>$</mo><mn>890</mn></math>. The value of the account doubled every <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> years. Which equation represents the value of the account <math alttext=\"upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math>, in dollars, <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> years after the account was opened?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"5f17b802-8420-486d-ac0b-126552f676bc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 890 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction t Over 10 EndFraction\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>890</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"e5669886-17bd-45fc-aa43-f22e092badde","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 890 left parenthesis one tenth right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction t Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>890</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"1c886297-e228-4cf7-9343-8c7871190b5a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper M left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 890 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscr