<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for graph of a curve" class="sr-only"><ul><li>In quadrant 2, the curve falls to its minimum at the point (0 comma 4).</li><li>In quadrant 1, the curve then rises.</li></ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The graph of the polynomial function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math>, where <math alttext="y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, is shown. The <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph is <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["4"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math>. The <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph of a function in the <em>xy</em>-plane is the point where the graph intersects the <em>y</em>-axis. The graph of the polynomial function shown intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 4 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. It's given that the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"5f07b257","external_id":"d6f230e9-a5fd-4506-837c-cde890c380bc","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"de42db77-30e0-41fe-a371-1e07ab601010","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 287.764248 275.22\" width=\"287.764248pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Graph of a curve in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from negative 1 to 1. The y axis ranges from negative 1 to 12. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stro