</defs>\n    <g clip-path=\"url(#p5e1593f52f)\">\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"142.698403\" xlink:href=\"#m6d67395785\" y=\"169.165362\"></use>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_2\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p5e1593f52f)\" d=\"M 59.649038 38.120605 \nL 61.751554 56.808021 \nL 63.854069 73.219846 \nL 65.956585 87.583378 \nL 68.0591 100.108444 \nL 69.741113 108.935215 \nL 71.423125 116.801067 \nL 73.105138 123.791574 \nL 74.78715 129.986465 \nL 76.469163 135.459891 \nL 78.151175 140.280698 \nL 79.833188 144.512679 \nL 81.5152 148.214833 \nL 83.197212 151.441609 \nL 84.879225 154.243149 \nL 86.561237 156.665517 \nL 88.24325 158.750929 \nL 89.925262 160.537973 \nL 91.607275 162.061824 \nL 93.70979 163.644936 \nL 95.812306 164.922429 \nL 97.914821 165.943443 \nL 100.43784 166.890195 \nL 102.960859 167.5928 \nL 105.904381 168.174381 \nL 109.268405 168.607894 \nL 113.473437 168.916519 \nL 119.36048 169.10083 \nL 130.293561 169.163907 \nL 167.297835 169.076861 \nL 173.184879 168.844702 \nL 177.38991 168.469152 \nL 180.753935 167.952229 \nL 183.697457 167.268461 \nL 186.220475 166.451054 \nL 188.322991 165.562933 \nL 190.425506 164.444817 \nL 192.528022 163.051338 \nL 194.210035 161.703735 \nL 195.892047 160.117204 \nL 197.574059 158.258995 \nL 199.256072 156.0931 \nL 200.938084 153.580044 \nL 202.620097 150.676668 \nL 204.302109 147.335912 \nL 205.984122 143.50658 \nL 207.666134 139.133107 \nL 209.348147 134.155319 \nL 211.030159 128.508183 \nL 212.712172 122.121553 \nL 214.394184 114.919908 \nL 216.076196 106.822084 \nL 217.758209 97.741 \nL 219.440221 87.583378 \nL 221.122234 76.249456 \nL 222.804246 63.632691 \nL 224.486259 49.619463 \nL 225.747768 38.120605 \nL 225.747768 38.120605 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p5e1593f52f\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"268.898496\" x=\"7.2\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a curve\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>In quadrant 2, the curve falls to its minimum at the point (0 comma 4).</li><li>In quadrant 1, the curve then rises.</li></ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of the polynomial function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, is shown. The <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["4"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math>. The <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph of a function in the <em>xy</em>-plane is the point where the graph intersects the <em>y</em>-axis. The graph of the polynomial function shown intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 4 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. It's given that the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math>.</p>","externalid":"d6f230e9-a5fd-4506-837c-cde890c380bc","correct_answer":["4"]},"createDate":1776362727993,"updateDate":1776362727993}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727993, 1776362727993),
    ($SATQ$6011a3f8$SATQ$, $SATQ$47af8694-05ad-4849-a1fb-69bbee9cc524$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$cd2e33cb-4c7b-405a-b0aa-9384b114f5f4$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="64 x squared plus b x plus 25 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
